
The fractional part of the cube root of 2 is : 428A2F98D728AE22

The decimal value for the cube root is 1.25992104989487316476721060727823

Simply multiply by 16 and use the integer part of the result for each
hexadecimal character and then use the remainder in the next multiply
operation : 

alpha $ echo '0.25992104989487316476721060727823 16* pq' | dc 
4.15873679831797063627536971645168
^
  ^-------------+
                |
                v-- fractional stuff from above
alpha $ echo '0.15873679831797063627536971645168 16* pq' | dc 
2.53978877308753018040591546322688
^
  ^-------------+
                |
                v-- fractional stuff from above
alpha $ echo '0.53978877308753018040591546322688 16* pq' | dc 
8.63662036940048288649464741163008

alpha $ echo '0.63662036940048288649464741163008 16* pq' | dc 
10.18592591040772618391435858608128
^
|
+---> this is hex digit A

alpha $ echo '0.18592591040772618391435858608128 16* pq' | dc 
2.97481456652361894262973737730048

alpha $ echo '0.97481456652361894262973737730048 16* pq' | dc 
15.59703306437790308207579803680768
^
|
+---> hex digit F

alpha $ echo '0.59703306437790308207579803680768 16* pq' | dc 
9.55252903004644931321276858892288

alpha $ echo '0.55252903004644931321276858892288 16* pq' | dc 
8.84046448074318901140429742276608

alpha $ echo '0.84046448074318901140429742276608 16* pq' | dc
13.44743169189102418246875876425728
^
|
+---> hex digit D

alpha $ echo '0.44743169189102418246875876425728 16* pq' | dc
7.15890707025638691950014022811648

alpha $ echo '0.15890707025638691950014022811648 16* pq' | dc
2.54251312410219071200224364986368

alpha $ echo '0.54251312410219071200224364986368 16* pq' | dc
8.68020998563505139203589839781888

alpha $ echo '0.68020998563505139203589839781888 16* pq' | dc
10.88335977016082227257437436510208

alpha $ echo '0.88335977016082227257437436510208 16* pq' | dc
14.13375632257315636118998984163328

alpha $ echo '0.13375632257315636118998984163328 16* pq' | dc
2.14010116117050177903983746613248

alpha $ echo '0.14010116117050177903983746613248 16* pq' | dc
2.24161857872802846463739945811968


The above sequence is 4  2  8 10  2 15  9  8 13  7  2  8 10 14  2  2
       the hex result 4  2  8  A  2  F  9  8  D  7  2  8  A  E  2  2

Thus the fractional part of the cube root of 2 is 0x428A2F98D728AE22

--------------------------------------------------------------------
   * * *   R o u n d i n g    E r r o r   * * *

We may see a rounding error on the last digit in the 16 hex digits.
An example of a rounding error would be seen in the cube root of 3.

First question is the cube root of 3 which is e^(ln(3)/3) :

hydra$ bc -lq
scale=48
e(l(3)/3)
1.442249570307408382321638310780109588391869253498

Then we take the fractional part and begin :

                    442249570307408382321638310780109588391869253498

phobos$ echo '40k 0.44224957030740838232873296531622 16* pq' | dc 
7.07599312491853411725972744505952
phobos$ echo '40k 0.07599312491853411725972744505952 16* pq' | dc 
1.21588999869654587615563912095232
phobos$ echo '40k 0.21588999869654587615563912095232 16* pq' | dc 
3.45423997914473401849022593523712
phobos$ echo '40k 0.45423997914473401849022593523712 16* pq' | dc 
7.26783966631574429584361496379392
phobos$ echo '40k 0.26783966631574429584361496379392 16* pq' | dc 
4.28543466105190873349783942070272
phobos$ echo '40k 0.28543466105190873349783942070272 16* pq' | dc 
4.56695457683053973596543073124352
phobos$ echo '40k 0.56695457683053973596543073124352 16* pq' | dc 
9.07127322928863577544689169989632
phobos$ echo '40k 0.07127322928863577544689169989632 16* pq' | dc 
1.14037166861817240715026719834112
phobos$ echo '40k 0.14037166861817240715026719834112 16* pq' | dc 
2.24594669789075851440427517345792
phobos$ echo '40k 0.24594669789075851440427517345792 16* pq' | dc 
3.93514716625213623046840277532672
phobos$ echo '40k 0.93514716625213623046840277532672 16* pq' | dc 
14.96235466003417968749444440522752
phobos$ echo '40k 0..96235466003417968749444440522752 16* pq' | dc 
15.39767456054687499991111048364032
phobos$ echo '40k 0.39767456054687499991111048364032 16* pq' | dc 
6.36279296874999999857776773824512
phobos$ echo '40k 0.36279296874999999857776773824512 16* pq' | dc 
5.80468749999999997724428381192192
phobos$ echo '40k 0.80468749999999997724428381192192 16* pq' | dc 
12.87499999999999963590854099075072
phobos$ echo '40k 0.87499999999999963590854099075072 16* pq' | dc 
13.99999999999999417453665585201152

Therefore the integer portion is actually 13 but we should round
up to 14 due to the 0.999999999999994174... fractional component.

The result above is 7137449123EF65CD with the final hex digit
being clearly a "D" value for 13.  The correct value should 
be 7137449123EF65CE where the trailing "E" is the result of
the x86 extended precision bullshit datatype only giving us
63 bits and not the 64 we need.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-------------- a closer look at the 80-bit x86 extended precision bullshit 


After a close look at the x86 80-bit extended precision data for a trivial
cube root we see that there is no way possible to get 64-bits of fractional
data. 

within a debugger we may look at the actual in memory data for cube root
of 3.0 thus :  ( note that gg is an alias for gdb with a dumb term )

phobos$ gg cube_roots
Reading symbols from cube_roots...
(gdb) break 184
Breakpoint 1 at 0x20282e: file cube_roots.c, line 184.
(gdb) run
Starting program: /usr/home/dclarke/pgm/bw/rfc4634_code/cube_roots 

Expect this to fail terribly as we lose precision
There is no way to squeeze 64 bits out of 53 bits.
---------------- 64-bit double type ---------------
    p    64-bit cube root                Reference Hex       Computed Hex
-------------------------------------------------------------------------
    2    1.25992104989487319067e+00      428A2F98D728AE22    428A2F98D728B000    ERROR
    3    1.44224957030740830177e+00      7137449123EF65CD    7137449123EF6000    ERROR
    5    1.70997594667669705615e+00      B5C0FBCFEC4D3B2F    B5C0FBCFEC4D4000    ERROR
    7    1.91293118277238916036e+00      E9B5DBA58189DBBC    E9B5DBA58189E000    ERROR
   11    2.22398009056931567073e+00      3956C25BF348B538    3956C25BF348C000    ERROR
   13    2.35133468772075771014e+00      59F111F1B605D019    59F111F1B605E000    ERROR
   17    2.57128159065823513885e+00      923F82A4AF194F9B    923F82A4AF194000    ERROR
   19    2.66840164872194485213e+00      AB1C5ED5DA6D8118    AB1C5ED5DA6D8000    ERROR
---------------- 128-bit double type? -------------
    p    128-bit cube root                           Reference Hex       Computed Hex
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Breakpoint 1, main (argc=1, argv=0x7fffffffe810) at cube_roots.c:184
184             cuberoot_ld = cbrtl((long double)p[j]);
(gdb) cont
Continuing.
    2    1.25992104989487316475411243787974e+00      428A2F98D728AE22    428A2F98D728AE22

Breakpoint 1, main (argc=1, argv=0x7fffffffe810) at cube_roots.c:184
184             cuberoot_ld = cbrtl((long double)p[j]);
(gdb) next
185             printf ("  %3i    %-40.32Le    %s    ", p[j], cuberoot_ld,hpf[j]);
(gdb) print cuberoot_ld 
$1 = 1.44224957030740838233
(gdb) print &cuberoot_ld 
$2 = (long double *) 0x7fffffffe770
(gdb) x/16xb 0x7fffffffe770
0x7fffffffe770: 0xe7    0xb2    0xf7    0x91    0x48    0xa2    0x9b    0xb8
0x7fffffffe778: 0xff    0x3f    0xff    0xff    0xff    0x7f    0x00    0x00
(gdb) quit
A debugging session is active.

        Inferior 1 [process 56268] will be killed.

Quit anyway? (y or n) y
phobos$ 

Above we see that the floating point value for the cube root of 3.0 is about 
somewhere in the vicinity of 1.44224957030740838233 which is in memory at
address 0x7fffffffe770.  This is 10 bytes or 80-bits in little endian order
and this the actual data is : 

    0xe7  0xb2  0xf7  0x91  0x48  0xa2  0x9b  0xb8  0xff  0x3f   

Which we can reverse and see as : 3FFFB89BA24891F7B2E7

The old desktop calc tool will give us the bits and we must be careful to
note that the leading nibble is 3 where 0011 binary is needed : 

phobos$ echo ' 16i 2o 3FFFB89BA24891F7B2E7 pq' | dc 
11111111111111101110001001101110100010010010001001000111110111101100101110011\
1
 
 
Thus the full binary data is :

            0011 1111 1111 1111 1011 1000 1001 1011 1010 0010 0100 1000 1001 0001 1111 0111 1011 0010 1110 0111
                                ^ Normalized value. 

A close look at the hexadecimal data reveals that the final digit is in fact E : 

                                 0111 0001  0011 0111 0100 0100 1001 0001 0010 0011 1110 1111 0110 0101 1100 111   
                                    7    1     3    7    4    4    9    1    2    3    E    F    6    5    C    D 

We know from RFC-4634 that the correct fractional hex data for the cube root of 3.0 is 
the byte sequence 7137449123EF65CD and clearly we have lost a bit of data from the above.

Thus the x86 hardware can not, ever, correctly compute the RFC-4634 data. Any attempt to
do so results in an error : 


    3    1.44224957030740838232873296531622e+00      7137449123EF65CD    7137449123EF65CE    ERROR

